+If your Service declares a custom command (via ``__command__``), BentoML serves it through an in-process reverse proxy that forwards incoming requests to the HTTP server started by that command. Use ``proxy_port`` to tell BentoML which port the custom command's server binds to. It defaults to ``8000``:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    @bentoml.service(http={"proxy_port": 8000})
+    class MyService:
+        # Service implementation
+
